  bit of edge over franklin and i suppose  that's because even though we've only  seen him in action once his abilities  are pretty damn amazing because may i  remind you that he conjured the planet  jupiter from his body holes which is  still one of the more devastating  attacks that we've ever seen however at  the same time bonolonov is a something  of an acquired taste in terms of design  i can see why so many people would just  plonk him into last place because he  doesn't look smart and smooth i mean he  is what he is and i guess what he is is  13th place on the opposite end of the  aesthetic scale now we have pretty boy  shalnock in 12th overall not scoring too  differently to bernal enough however and  this surprised me the majority of  placements for shao knock ended up in  the 10th to 14th range and that shocks  me because i'd always thought that  shalnok was a lot more popular than that  maybe sitting at seventh or eighth but i  guess that's just my anecdotal  experience i suppose what might tank  charnock is his less than original  inability and while his design is that's  quite typically appealing it might be a  tad too generic especially in a group  full of all sorts of wacky weirdos  including headweirdo crollo and deputy  head weirdo hisoka it's very difficult  to sit beside those two and have any  chance of standing out still it  intrigues me because number eleven  defeating shanak is kaluto zoldik and if  i had to guess what this ranking would  be out of thin air i probably would have  placed calito in 14th or maybe even last  place but kalito has an almost banalinov  style effect happening here because if  you look at his percentages from fifth  to tenth place it is astoundingly  uniform like you go five percent then  six six six seven seven whereas most  characters have a solid one or two  numbers that the majority of voters pile  into but not carlito which i think shows  that people on average do appreciate  color toe quite a bit although carlito  did receive around 10 percent of all  last place votes  there's also that but this is why we do  ranked choice polls because kalato would  never stand a chance if we just asked  what everyone's number one favorite is  so this is quite revealing of the true  feelings of the hunt hunter fandom it's  a form of fan-based mind-reading not too  dissimilar from the abilities of our  10th place contender parkunoda and this  is where we start to see a noticeable  shift at the top end of voting because  pakunoda received 221 first place  finishes which no it's not much but it's  more than double what kaloto received so  whilst the majority of votes do still  lie in the 10th to 14th range for  pakunoda there is a significant enough  cohort of people placing her in first to  third that just gets her over the line  here and i'd say that the obvious reason  for that is because she's one of the few  troop members to have had a complete  character arc which did result in one of  the more tragic and bittersweet deaths  in hunter hunter pakunoda is memorable  and also memorable because she does have  very pronounced boob things which as  much as i would like to think otherwise  yeah look it probably also played a part  in her support we are taking another big  leap forward now with number nine to  discover one shizuku who not only  finally breaks the two percent barrier  for first place votes but also has the  least amount of last place finishes so  far only 198 people rank shizuku and  15th which is one of the lowest  proportions of any troop member in fact  there are only three members who receive  less last-place votes than shizuku but  shizuku is also well she's kind of right  where she belongs because over 50 people  did place her between 7th to 11th so you  know 9th that sounds like a pretty  lovely middle ground and my general  conclusion here is  what's not to love about shizuku she  might not have the flair to compete with  the true favorites but there's very few  reasons 