ause over 50 percent of all of  you think that things land somewhere  between third and eighth place thinks is  he's actually kind of stupidly popular  but you would never know that from a  poll that only asks for your number one  favorite so good on you thinks my gum  getting into serious business now this  is the upper third and it all kicks off  with machi not too surprising because in  my experience marcia has always been  held as a top-end favorite because she  kind of has it all cool design fun  string based none ability and even some  high emotional stakes in the story being  directly connected to hisoka  interestingly machi's votes are most  heavily weighted in the 5th to 8th place  range however what kicks her into the  top of that is the complete and utter  lack of lower end placements for example  a grand total of 80 people put marchi in  last place then another 130 put her into  14th and only 246 decided that marche  should be even 13th these are incredibly  low numbers and that's actually the  primary reason as to how machi secured  victory over things meanwhile in fourth  place lands illumi zoldick and franime  only fans just quickly yes ilami is  indeed a member of the troop he joined  in the manga shortly after the anime  events concluded and while we could ask  whether it's fair or not to include such  a prolific character on this poll my  hands are kind of tied on the issue he  is a member so i can't really leave him  out and people do have very strong and  consistent feelings towards hillary with  a whopping 17 of all voters slamming him  straight into third place that is the  highest concentration of voters we've  seen so far apart from cortopia's  unfortunate last place and dilemma also  performs exceptionally well in fourth  and fifth positions as well however only  327 people voted to put him into first  which is less than march he thinks and  even shizuku received so in a more  standard pick the favorite poll ilmi  would end up being more like seventh  place but i certainly think that this is  more accurate to award the bronze medal  now i asked feitan porter to step up  into the third place position podium now  feitan is the first character on this  ranking to actually break a 10 point  average which is kind of shocking but i  think it reflects how top heavy  preferences are for our final three now  fake tan certainly is a popular little  rascal with almost 40 voters ranking him  somewhere between first and third but  i'm actually surprised that that wasn't  higher particularly in the first place  sector only  1294 four people elected to hold feitan  as their number one which is  astoundingly higher than anyone else so  far yes but it does pale pretty  radically in comparison to the top two  and with that we announce our second  place finisher being hisoka with a total  of over 4 800 votes in first place and a  staggering 73 percent of all voters  ranking him somewhere between first and  third is this to be expected i mean yes  i guess it is hisoka generally the sword  of paul will always come down to a  battle between crolo and hisoka although  it is very interesting to note that  there are indeed a small portion of  dissenters within the hisoka camp just  over three percent of all people put  hisoka in last place which may not sound  like much but it is actually huge  compared to both feitan and crowler who  received more like half a percent and to  be fair hisoka he can be a controversial  character and i suppose it might even be  surprising that so few people put him in  last place but that of course leads us  into crowning our grand champion who is  of course crolo lucifer however i want  to point out something very very major  here which is that crollo actually  received less first place votes than  hisoka did over 300 or so less so if  this was your standard favorite poll  hisoka would have won and this is why  ranked choice voting is ever so  important it goes whilst there may be  more hardcore